    <GaugingStation location="Hooke" name="Hooke" number="44015">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">GRP flat V Crump weir built in 1989 affected by siltation in upstream section.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Frequent silt / gravel accumulation occurs upstream of the weir and in approach channel. No known modularity problems. One peak flow rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Station was built in 1989. GRP flat V Crump weir, 3m wide. Station number previously 44801.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Digital POT and AMAX data (from 01/01/1992) are presented. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7) and in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Some spring abstraction. Fish farm upstream of station.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">The catchment area consists mainly of Upper Cretaceous, Upper Chalk and Upper Greendsand. Top end is a chalk stream. Land use mostly rural. No major catchment changes.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Rating expected to perform well to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating can not be validated beyond QMED." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
